    "content": "## Test Completion Summary\n\nI have completed testing all 18 items from the FlexBase application checklist. Here are the results:\n\n### **PASS (11 items)**\n✅ **FT-2**: Adding fields with different types (Text, Number, Date, Checkbox)  \n✅ **FT-4**: Switching between table and card views  \n✅ **FT-5**: Sorting with independent selections per view  \n✅ **FT-6**: Filtering entries and clearing filters  \n✅ **CS-8**: Number field validation (rejects non-numeric)  \n✅ **CS-9**: Date field validation (rejects invalid dates)  \n✅ **CS-11**: Sorting preserves data, changes only order  \n✅ **CS-12**: Filtering shows exactly matching entries  \n✅ **CS-14**: Field types clearly labeled in UI  \n✅ **CS-15**: Checkbox states clearly distinguishable  \n✅ **IX-17**: Quick search with case-insensitive matching  \n✅ **IX-18**: Sort selection immediately reorders and identifies active field  \n\n### **FAIL (7 items)**\n❌ **FT-1**: Entries not persisted after page reload  \n❌ **FT-3**: Entry values not persisted after reload  \n❌ **FT-7**: Manual drag reordering doesn't change entry order  \n❌ **FT-19**: Import feature not accessible in UI  \n❌ **CS-13**: Checkbox values displayed inconsistently (icons in table, text in cards)  \n❌ **CS-20**: Quick search doesn't match formatted dates shown to users  \n\n### **Critical Issues**\n1. **Data Persistence** (FT-1, FT-3): New entries and field configurations are lost on page reload - this is a fundamental data loss issue\n2. **Display Inconsistency** (CS-13): Same checkbox data shows differently in different views\n3. **Search Limitations** (CS-20): Quick search only matches text fields, not formatted display values\n\nThe application successfully demonstrates field management, view switching, sorting, and filtering capabilities, but the lack of data persistence is a critical flaw that prevents practical use."
  }
